      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update dotnet8-runtime to 8.0.34-r0 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-70175 (GHSA-x3vp-85cm-q97r) is an ASP.NET Core elevation of privilege issue in ASP.NET Core Identity: password-reset and confirmation flows can send mail to the address supplied in the request instead of the user's stored address. Microsoft's original advisory lists the ASP.NET Core 8.0 runtime packs, including linux-musl-x64 and linux-musl-arm64, as affected from 8.0.0 through 8.0.31 and fixed in 8.0.32. Its November update adds the Identity UI and Blazor template code shipped in the .NET SDK, listing .NET SDK 8.0.100 through 8.0.133 as affected and 8.0.134 as fixed for the 8.0.1xx feature band, and notes that application code generated from earlier templates must be repaired separately (https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/security/advisories/GHSA-x3vp-85cm-q97r, https://github.com/dotnet/announcements/issues/457, https://github.com/dotnet/core/blob/main/release-notes/8.0/8.0.32/8.0.32.md, https://github.com/dotnet/core/blob/main/release-notes/8.0/8.0.34/8.0.34.md). DHI dotnet8-runtime for Alpine 3.23 builds .NET 8 for Linux from Microsoft's source release, and each build's version is the .NET runtime version it carries. Scanned all 220 packages of the ten published builds (8.0.23-r0, 8.0.24-r0, 8.0.25-r0, 8.0.26-r0, 8.0.27-r0, 8.0.29-r0, 8.0.31-r0, 8.0.32-r0, 8.0.33-r0 and 8.0.34-r0) for x86_64 and aarch64, including the files inside the nupkg and other zip archives they hold: every build ships Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity.dll at its own .NET version, in the ASP.NET Core shared framework of aspnetcore8-runtime and of the .NET SDK held by dotnet8-runtime-bootstrap and in the ASP.NET Core runtime pack held by dotnet8-runtime-bootstrap, plus reference assemblies with no implementation code (including 6.0.2 reference assemblies in source-build reference packages); the .NET SDK held by dotnet8-runtime-bootstrap is 8.0.1NN in build 8.0.NN-r0 and includes the ASP.NET Core web project templates. So 8.0.23-r0 to 8.0.31-r0 carry the unfixed Identity runtime, and 8.0.32-r0 and 8.0.33-r0 carry SDKs 8.0.132 and 8.0.133, which the November update lists as affected. The range ends at 8.0.34-r0 because it is the first published build whose runtime and SDK both carry the fix."
    },
